<p>What the figure shows: Akmola jumps from 10.8 to 49.6, North Kazakhstan from 0 to 24.0 and Mangistau from 0 to 11.6, while Kostanay falls from 34.1 to 12.6. These swings are what small numbers look like. Zhetisu (36.5 to 51.0) and Ulytau (29.6 to 34.6) are the exceptions that stay high, which makes them better candidates for a targeted pilot than regions that spiked once.</p>
